-- DEFECT P4. Amendment 15 to the National Health Insurance Law, Sefer HaChukim 1798 p. 433 (19 July 2001 = 28 Tammuz 5761), s 1(1), changes s 58 of the Law, paragraph (1) of the definition of an absence year.
-- It replaces one pair, a Hebrew date and a Gregorian date for one day, by another pair. The old pair names one day. The new pair does not: 14 Adar 5761 is 9 March 2001, and 1 March 2001 is 6 Adar 5761.
-- Both conversions were made with the calendar routine, which reproduced 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024 first. Only s 1(1) of the page is quoted; nothing else on it is.
