`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day` MEANS
    `A day given twice` WITH
        `the words giving the day are in` IS "Sefer HaChukim 1798 p. 433, s 1(1), the words inserted in s 58(א), paragraph (1) of the definition of an absence year"
        `the Hebrew date names` IS Date 9 3 2001
        `the Gregorian date names` IS Date 1 3 2001
        `the consolidation prints the same pair` IS TRUE
        `read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- CONTROL for P4. The pair that the same instruction replaces: 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999 name one day (13 Adar 5759 = 1 March 1999 by the calendar routine).
-- The consolidation no longer prints it (a search of the deposited consolidation finds no occurrence of the Hebrew date).
`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day` MEANS
    `A day given twice` WITH
        `the words giving the day are in` IS "Sefer HaChukim 1798 p. 433, s 1(1), the words replaced in s 58(א), paragraph (1) of the definition of an absence year"
        `the Hebrew date names` IS Date 1 3 1999
        `the Gregorian date names` IS Date 1 3 1999
        `the consolidation prints the same pair` IS FALSE
        `read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
